            "text": "{\n  \"verdict\": \"ACCEPTED\",\n  \"reconstruction\": [\n    \"Theorem 18.2(b), (c), (e): VERIFIED. The translation invariance of the Borel probability measure correctly gives the transfer criterion. The supremum bound $C_\\\\nu(d) = \\\\sup_t \\\\nu((t-d,t]) \u003e 0$ is exact and holds for any Borel probability law because the real line can be partitioned into intervals of length $d$, and at least one must have positive measure. Sufficiency fails under correlated background, as demonstrated.\",\n    \"Proposition 18.3(d): VERIFIED. The total variation $TV(\\\\nu, \\\\nu * \\\\delta_g)$ equals $\\\\nu(\\\\{0\\\\})$ if and only if the signed measure $\\\\nu - \\\\nu * \\\\delta_g$ has no positive mass on $(0, \\\\infty)$. By domination, this forces $\\\\nu$ to be supported on $g\\\\mathbb{Z}_{\\\\ge 0}$ with nonincreasing weights.\",\n    \"Proposition 18.4(c): VERIFIED. Trace preservation for Kraus operators mapping basis states to pure outputs forces the Kraus coefficient vectors to be orthonormal within each fiber. Thus, the Kraus rank is bounded below by the maximum fiber size. Non-singleton fibers imply logical irreversibility.\",\n    \"Proposition 19.1(a)-(c): VERIFIED. The center of the commutative algebra $A_X$ consists of single configurations. The P1 pullback $P(j,x) = j+x$ is not injective on $\\\\{0,1\\\\} \\\\times \\\\{0,1\\\\}$, so the center is not retained. The dilated register $B(H_p')$ has a trivial center.\",\n    \"Lemma 19.3: VERIFIED. The Gram matrix parametrization $G_{bb'}$ for extensions of a classical map correctly captures all CPTP extensions, with $G_{bb'} = \\\\delta_{bb'}$ within fibers due to trace preservation.\",\n    \"Theorem 19.4(a)-(d): VERIFIED. The event-determined effects are exactly those whose matrix elements vanish between distinct reachable classical outputs, which forms the diagonal algebra $D(\\\\Omega')$. The receiver-local part is $C^*(N_p')$.\",\n    \"Corrected Corollary 19.5: VERIFIED. The conditions (A1) locality, (A2) event determinacy, and (A3) completeness are necessary and sufficient for $A_{av} = D_p$. The text explicitly states that pre-event access and the native field-to-state association are assumed, not derived.\",\n    \"Witness 19.6: VERIFIED. The hand-computed expectations for $\\\\Phi_{can}$ and $\\\\Phi_{alt}$ on coherent inputs $\\\\psi_1$ and $\\\\psi_2$ yield the stated values (0 and 1, swapped), confirming that the coherent extensions disagree on off-diagonal elements.\",\n    \"Controls 19.7: VERIFIED. Supplying a single extension trivially determines all expectations. Genesis dump fails to select the receiver. Without (A1), the joint algebra can use a reference. The center route fails. Unit-freeness is required to select $Q$.\",\n    \"Proposition 19.8(a)-(d): VERIFIED. The ancestry-retention contract $R$ on the elementary step class yields the triangular system $\\\\sum_{d \\\\le j} w_d = 1$, which uniquely forces $w = e_1$ (the P1 step). With positivity, $E2$ and $R_p$ alone force $w = e_1$. Without positivity, $w = (1, 1, -1)$ is a valid counterexample.\",\n    \"Premise (A0): VERIFIED. The assumption that availability forms an algebra is explicitly declared as a premise.\",\n    \"Lemma 20.1: VERIFIED. Finite-dimensional commutative C*-algebras are exactly the partition algebras $\\\\sigma(\\\\pi)$.\",\n    \"Theorem 20.2(a)-(d): VERIFIED. The available post-event state is the pushforward $\\\\pi_*$. The contrast is monotone under partition refinement (data processing). Incomparable partitions can be ordered either way, as shown by the threshold and parity partitions.\",\n    \"Theorem 20.3(a)-(c): VERIFIED. Scale-invariant functions on the half-line are constant on $(0, \\\\infty)$. Restricted to a finite reachable set containing 0 and a positive value, they span the two-dimensional algebra $C^*(Q_p)$. The premise (A3') forces this algebra.\",\n    \"Corollary 20.4(a)-(d): VERIFIED. The intertwining $Q_p K_i = K_i P$ follows directly from $N_{out} K_i = K_i N_{in}$ by applying the indicator function $1_{\u003e0}$. The transfer criterion $\\\\nu(\\\\{0\\\\}) \u003e 0$ is exact.\",\n    \"Controls 20.5: VERIFIED. Without (A3'), the trivial algebra gives 0 contrast. Without (U), any partition is sound. If $\\\\nu(\\\\{0\\\\}) = 0$, $Q$ is blind. Genesis dump gives 0 contrast at $p$.\",\n    \"Witnesses 20.6: VERIFIED. The hand-computed contrasts for the threshold, parity, and $Q$ partitions match the stated values, confirming the incomparability and optimality claims.\",\n    \"FOLLOWUP equations (1)-(6): VERIFIED. The binary effect $E = a(I-Q_p) + b Q_p$ yields the contrast $|b-a|\\\\nu(\\\\{0\\\\})$. The impossibility of obtaining $Q_p$ from $E$ via stochastic post-processing for $a=1/4, b=3/4$ is correct, as it would require probabilities outside $[0,1]$.\"\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"missing_assumptions\": [],\n  \"counterexamples\": [],\n  \"inserted_mechanisms\": [\n    \"(A0) Availability is an algebra (declared premise).\",\n    \"(A1) Receiver locality (declared premise).\",\n    \"(A2) Event determinacy / soundness (declared premise).\",\n    \"(A3) Completeness (declared premise).\",\n    \"(A3') Nontriviality (declared premise).\",\n    \"(U) Unit-freeness of records (declared premise).\",\n    \"E5 / E5+ for receiver selection (declared premise).\",\n    \"Occurrence of the pruning (declared existential input).\",\n    \"The declared preparation pair (declared premise).\",\n    \"Preparability G / N_1(l) (declared premise).\",\n    \"(H-J) Native field-to-state association (declared premise).\",\n    \"FOLLOWUP's response parameters a, b (declared as an open proof obligation, not chosen).\"\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"The construction does not claim a physical measurement model, decoherence dynamics, or einselection.\",\n    \"The identification of Q_p with the v15.16 sector Q_C of the frozen encoding remains an open obligation.\",\n    \"The native preparability of 